# Adding a directory integration (auto-launch)

**Agent:** One PR, [PR checklist](#pr-checklist). Not a social `SocialProvider` — profile in OpenQuok, member submits on the directory site; extension autofills from API `extension_config`. Social posting: **add-social-provider-integration.mdc**. Also **backend-migrations-naming**, **backend-migrations-seed**, **source-project-neutrality**, **company-brand-icons**.

**Deep reference:** `docs/auto-launch/extension-ui-patterns.md` (steps, compare rail, `profilePath` tables, manual smoke).

## Identifier contract

| Concept | Format | Must match in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Site slug** | kebab-case (`peerpush`, `open-launch`) | `link_directory_sites.slug`, bundled logo lists below, `web/static/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg` |
| **Opportunity slug** | per path (`standard-launch`, `free-queue`) | `link_directory_opportunities.slug` (per `site_id`) |
| **Provider slug** | `{site}-{variant}` | `auto_launch_destinations`, `link_directory_opportunities.auto_launch_provider_slug`, `destination-configs/<site>.ts` provider rows + aggregated `directoryLaunchProviders`, content script registration, tests |

Wire: `auto_launch_enabled` + `auto_launch_provider_slug` on opportunity; `auto_launch_destinations.link_directory_opportunity_id` → opportunity. Optional `picker_group_key` / `picker_group_title` for one Add Channel card with variant picker.

### Directory site logo (web dashboard + extension side panel)

One SVG per **site slug** under `web/static/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg`. When adding a shipped directory site, update **all three** slug lists together (same site slug in each):

| Surface | Path | Used by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Asset | `web/static/icons/link-directory/<site-slug>.svg` | Web `/icons/link-directory/…`, extension build copies from here |
| Web | `web/src/lib/auto-launch/buildDirectoryAddChannelTiles.ts` — `BUNDLED_DIRECTORY_LOGO_SLUGS`, `DIRECTORY_SITE_BRANDED_ICONS` | My Products Add Channel tiles |
| Extension | `extension/scripts/copy-static.mjs` — `shippedLinkDirectoryLogoSlugs` | Copies SVGs into `dist/icons/link-directory/` at build |
| Extension | `extension/scripts/verify-extension-dist.mjs` — `shippedLinkDirectoryLogoSlugs` | Fails build if any listed icon is missing from `dist/` |

The extension side panel loads `chrome.runtime.getURL('icons/link-directory/{siteKey}.svg')` (`directoryChannelPicker.ts`). If the SVG is not copied into the extension package, the avatar falls back to **two-letter site initials** (e.g. TinyLaunch → `TI`), not the real logo.

After edits: `pnpm --filter @openquok/browser-extension build` and confirm `dist/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg` exists. See also `buildDirectoryAddChannelTiles.test.ts` for web tile logo URLs.

## Files to add or modify

### Database (seeds)

| Action | Path | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Add | `backend/supabase/db/link-directory/504_<date>_seed_<site>.sql` | `link_directory_sites` + `link_directory_opportunities` (`dofollow`, cost, `auto_launch_*`) |
| Add | `backend/supabase/db/auto-launch/<prefix>_<date>_seed_<site>_destination.sql` | Destination rows; `extension_config` embedded on INSERT via `pnpm sync:auto-launch-destinations` (next prefix: **508+**; see tier note below) |
| Regenerate | `backend/supabase/db/auto-launch/502_*_extension_configs.sql` | Via `pnpm sync:auto-launch-configs` — do not hand-edit |
| Run | `pnpm sync:auto-launch-destinations` then `pnpm backend:db:aggregate-migrations-all` | Never edit `backend/supabase/migrations/*_core_structure.sql` |

**Tier 5xx order:** `502` extension_configs UPDATE (no-op on empty table) → `503`–`507` site `*_seed_*` files (`destinationSeeds.ts` manifest). **`507` = Fazier**; next site destination seed prefix: **508+** (do not add a second configs file).

Refs: Uneed `link-directory/502_*` + `auto-launch/503_*`; PeerPush `link-directory/504_*` + `auto-launch/504_*`; Open Launch `link-directory/505_*` + `auto-launch/505_*`; TinyLaunch catalog backfill + `auto-launch/506_*`; Fazier catalog backfill + `auto-launch/507_*`; DevHunt catalog backfill + `auto-launch/508_*`. Storage bucket: `auto-launch/500_*_seed_auto_launch_profile_media_bucket.sql` (reuse unless new bucket).

### Build Backlinks catalog backfill (JSON-only sites)

Some shipped directory sites exist only in the **Build Backlinks hub** catalog, not in a dedicated `link-directory/504_*_seed_<site>.sql` migration.

| Approach | When | Hub site + opportunities | Auto-launch destinations |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **SQL seed** | Default for new sites | `backend/supabase/db/link-directory/504_<date>_seed_<site>.sql` | `auto-launch/<prefix>_<date>_seed_<site>_destination.sql` |
| **Catalog JSON only** | Hub catalog is the source of truth (e.g. **TinyLaunch**, **Fazier**) | Append to `backend/scripts/link_directory_catalog_backfill.catalog.json` | Same `auto-launch/*_seed_*_destination.sql` via `destinationSeeds.ts` — **no** `link-directory/504_*` file |

For JSON-only sites:

1. Add a versioned `entries.<site-slug>` block in `link_directory_catalog_backfill.catalog.json` — stable UUIDs per site and opportunity rows; `auto_launch_enabled` + `auto_launch_provider_slug` on each opportunity; editorial copy (`dofollow`, cost, steps, `cta_href`, `openquok_cta_kind` as needed).
2. After deploy or local `supabase db reset`, run `pnpm backend:db:backfill-link-directory-catalog` (optional filter: `-- --slug <site-slug>`; use `--dry-run` first). Production: `pnpm backend:db:backfill-link-directory-catalog:prod`.
3. Operator notes: `web/src/content/docs/admin/link-directory-catalog-backfill.md`.

**Opportunity copy on `/build-backlinks/{site}`:** `description`, `cost_note`, and step `body` strings render through `prepareLinkDirectoryRichTextForDisplay`, which linkifies bare full `https://…` (or `http://…`) URLs to `host/path` anchor text. Use bare URLs for short destinations (for example `https://www.tinylaunch.com/pricing`). For long doc or store URLs, use `<a href="https://…">short label</a>` so the UI does not show a long path. Do not use bare hosts without a scheme (for example `fazier.com/page/new;`) — punctuation stays on the host and the text is not clickable. Keep blurbs short: one idea per sentence, active voice.

**Opportunity `effort` (Build Backlinks badges + site effort range):** set on each opportunity in SQL seeds or catalog JSON (`easy` | `medium` | `hard`).

| Pattern | Use `effort` | Reference opportunities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`cost_tier: free`** on shipped **directory / launch platforms** (free queue, free listing, free product path) | **`medium`** | PeerPush free queue, Open Launch free launch, TinyLaunch Standard, Fazier free product listing, DevHunt free listing |
| Paid checkout + typical submit wizard | **`medium`** | PeerPush Standard, DevHunt paid launch, Fazier paid tiers, Open Launch Premium |
| Chrome Web Store listing fields (package review, compliance copy, multi-tab listing editor) | **`hard`** | `official-url`, `item-homepage-url`, `privacy-policy-url` — **even when `cost_tier` is `free`** for a single field |

Put queue timing and approval delays in `approval_time_hint`, not in `effort`. Do not use **`hard`** on free-tier **launch-platform** opportunities. **Exception:** `chrome-web-store` in catalog backfill — all opportunities stay **`hard`**; that site is not a launch-platform row above.

