### Extension

| Action | Path |
| --- | --- |
| **Add** | `extension/src/content/directory-launch/<slug>.ts` — `registerDirectoryLaunchProvider('<provider_slug>')` (`contentScriptEntry` must match the row in `sites/<site>/config.ts`) |
| Edit | `extension/scripts/build-extension.mjs` — `contentScriptSpecs` |
| Edit | `extension/scripts/copy-static.mjs` + `verify-extension-dist.mjs` — append **site slug** to `shippedLinkDirectoryLogoSlugs` (keep in sync with web `BUNDLED_DIRECTORY_LOGO_SLUGS`) |
| Edit | `extension/manifest.json` — `content_scripts` `matches` + `js` |
| **Add** | `extension/src/directory/directory-launch/siteLogin/<site-key>.ts` + test |
| Edit | `extension/src/directory/directory-launch/siteLogin/detectDirectorySiteLogin.ts` — register adapter |
| **Add** (site-specific media DOM) | `extension/src/directory/directory-launch/siteMedia/<adapter>.ts` — implement `SiteMediaAdapter`; register in `siteMedia/registry.ts` |
| Edit (if DOM read fails) | `readFormField.ts`, `fillEngine.test.ts`, `readFormField.test.ts`, and a focused `*FormSelectors.test.ts` — **not** inline site branches in `fillEngine.ts` (see below) |
| Edit (generic DOM helpers) | `formFieldDom.ts` — neutral label/choice/url guards shared by fill + compare; **no** site slugs or brand names in identifiers or comments |

**`fillEngine.ts` stays generic.** Do not add directory-site logic there (no per-site hostnames or CDN URL heuristics, no site-named selectors, no site-specific gallery/logo upload loops). Use `extension_config` field hints (`selectorHint`, `maxItems`, catalogs) plus a `siteMedia/` adapter for DOM that generic fill cannot cover (multi-slot galleries, non-standard file inputs, preview image filtering). `fillEngine` delegates file resolution and multi-file fill through `getActiveSiteMediaAdapter()`; `readFormField` uses `getSiteMediaAdapterForGalleryPreview()` for gallery previews. Shared label/choice/promo-video DOM rules live in `formFieldDom.ts`. Catalog-driven fill (e.g. `tagsCatalog`) in `fillEngine` / `catalogTagsFill.ts` is fine — that is config, not page shape.

Build: `pnpm common:build` && `pnpm --filter @openquok/browser-extension build`.

